{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] |
| [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] | [Ebmaj7] | [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
He [Bb]prayed for friends who [Ebmaj7]spoke of blame
[Gm7]The Lord restored his lost [Ebmaj7]estate
[Bb]Twice as much as he had [Ebmaj7]known
A [Gm7]blessing greater than be[Ebmaj7]fore
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Shepherds counted flocks [Ebmaj7]in rows
[Gm7]Camels and oxen under [Ebmaj7]sun
[Bb]He saw his children [Ebmaj7]grow
And [Gm7]lived to [F]see the [Bb]fourth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Kezi[Eb]ah was his second [Bb]girl
A [Eb]name like spice that fills [Bb]the air
No [Eb]women matched their beauty [Gm7]there
His [Cm7]daughters shared [F7]the land [Bb]and care [Ebmaj7][Bb][Ebmaj7]
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]Jemimah led the [Ebmaj7]line
[Gm7]K-eren-hap-puch brought the [Ebmaj7]close
[Bb]Three sisters in his house of [Ebmaj7]joy
[Gm7]With [F]silver rings and [Bb]peace
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Kezi[Eb]ah was his second [Bb]girl
A [Eb]name like spice that fills [Bb]the air
No [Eb]women matched their beauty [Gm7]there
His [Cm7]daughters shared [F]the land [Bb]and care
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Interlude}
| [Ebmaj7] | [Ebmaj7] | [Gm7] | [Gm7] |
